    <bpmn:process id="W_W3819" name="W3819. Trade Competency Assessment, Practical Examination &amp; Certification Sign-Off" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Module/cohort completion (W3818)
Frequency: Per assessment event
Volume: Apprentice assessments
Owner: Trade Capability / Master Tradespersons
Participants: Trade Capability, Master Tradespersons/Assessors (links to W3828), L&amp;D (links to VS-19.4/W683), Compliance (links to VS-22), Quality (links to VS-31), TESDA (links to W3811)
Source: workflow W3819 — Trade Competency Assessment, Practical Examination &amp; Certification Sign-Off</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3819_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3819_Lane1" name="Trade Capability">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3819_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3819_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3819_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3819_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3819_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3819_Start3" name="Module/cohort completion (W3818)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3819_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3819_Task4" name="Trade Capability/Master-Tradespersons run competency assessments per the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Trade Capability/Master-Tradespersons run competency assessments per the curriculum (links to W3810): written/theory, practical demonstration (e.g., cut-and-measure lumber board-foot, lay a tile sample, fit a pipe joint, tint a paint sample, safe power-tool operation), and structured scoring
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / Master Tradespersons
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: Per assessment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3819_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3819_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3819_Task5" name="Trade Capability/Compliance coordinate TESDA NC/COC assessment where applicable…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Trade Capability/Compliance coordinate TESDA NC/COC assessment where applicable (links to W3811), ensure assessor qualification and assessment-center standards, and capture results/certification (links to W3815)
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / Compliance / L&amp;D
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: Per assessment</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3819_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3819_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3819_Task6" name="Trade Capability issue BuildRight internal trade certification and TESDA…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Trade Capability issue BuildRight internal trade certification and TESDA certification (links to W3815), manage re-assessment/remediation for not-yet-competent apprentices (links to W3821), and feed results into placement (links to W3822)
Responsible (R): Trade Capability / L&amp;D
Accountable (A): Trade Capability Lead
Duration: On certification</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3819_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3819_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3819_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3819_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3819_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-125 (ensure apprenticeship statutory compliance.) | - operational: standards and assessor qualification (links to W3828); operational: remediation pathway
Owner: Trade Capability / Master Tradespersons</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
